54/georgia-ag-asks-sec-take-action-vs-lsu-expulsion","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Mark Schlabach and Pete Thamel","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Alabama running back prospect AK Dear no longer with team","description":"Alabama tailback AK Dear, a former four-star prospect who was poised to make an impact before suffering an injury in the summer, is no longer on the team.","published":"2026-11-18T19:16:16.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50523034/alabama-running-back-prospect-ak-dear-no-longer-team","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Judge questions LSU's claims the SEC 'hallucinated' citations","description":"At a hearing Wednesday in the SEC's lawsuit against LSU, a federal judge pushed back on LSU attorneys for using the word \"hallucinated\" in filing.","published":"2026-11-18T22:40:51.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50522883/judge-questions-lsu-claims-sec-hallucinated-citations","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2027 College Football Playoff National Championship odds","description":"Odds and futures to win the 2027 College Football Playoff National Championship.","published":"2026-11-18T22:17:13.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/47664633/2027-college-football-playoff-national-championship-odds-futures","type":"Story","byline":"Doug Greenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Sources: Urban Meyer not a candidate for open Maryland job","description":"Urban Meyer has not spoken to Maryland in any formal capacity about its vacant head coaching position and is not a candidate for the job, sources told ESPN's Pete Thamel on Wednesday.","published":"2026-11-18T18:30:02.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50522632/sources-urban-meyer-not-candidate-open-maryland-job","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Davenport RB Cephus Harris III to enter transfer portal","description":"Davenport's Cephus Harris III, the leading rusher in Division II and a candidate for the Harlon Hill Trophy, plans to enter the transfer portal, he told ESPN.","published":"2026-11-18T17:52:53.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50522473/davenport-rb-cephus-harris-iii-enter-transfer-portal","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Top 25 betting lines: UGA big faves over Gamecocks, Vols slim favorites vs. LSU","description":"This week's odds and FPI predictions for South Carolina-Georgia, Tennessee-LSU and more.","published":"2026-11-18T14:36:40.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/50498153/2026-college-football-week-12-top-25-betting-lines-odds","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5226976/romanas-frederique-jr","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OJ_Frederique_Jr."},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"OJ Frederique Jr.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OJ_Frederique_Jr.","description":"American football player","touched":"2026-11-14T07:36:34Z","intro":"Romanas 'OJ' Frederique Jr. is an American college football cornerback for the Miami Hurricanes.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Frederique attended St. Thomas Aquinas High School in Fort Lauderdale, Florida. Coming out of high school, he was rated as a three-star recruit and held offers from schools such as Florida State, Miami, Ole Miss, UCF, and West Virginia. Frederique committed to play college football for the West Virginia Mountaineers. However, he flipped his commitment to the Miami Hurricanes."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Frederique got his first career start in week two of the 2024 season, where he recorded two tackles and a pass deflection in a win over Florida A&M. In week nine, he recorded a tackle and a pass deflection in a win over Florida State. In week 11, Frederique tallied five tackles and two pass deflections in a loss to Georgia Tech."}]}}